{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Getting the Job You Want"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Make It Happen"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future Continuous Tense vs. The Future Perfect Tense "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future Continuous tense to express actions that occur over a period of time in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will be working</span> at 4 p.m. tomorrow. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The person will start work at some point in the future and still be working at 4 p.m. It is not clear when the person will stop working. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of the Future Continuous is: <br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">will</span> + <span class=\"italic\">be</span> + verb <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">They<span class=\"strong\">'ll be doing</span> something wrong.</span><p>*It is common to use contractions in conversation (<span class=\"italic\">They will</span> = <span class=\"italic\">They'll</span>).</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " You use the Future Perfect tense to express future actions that take place before a different action in the future.  The Future Perfect is somewhat like the Present Perfect tense, but the perspective is the future, not the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">We can have lunch at 12 p.m. tomorrow. I <span class=\"strong\">will have finished</span> the meeting.  <br/>The bus will leave the terminus at 10 a.m. You will arrive at 11:15 a.m. At that time, the bus <span class=\"strong\">will have left</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of the Future Perfect tense is: <br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">will </span>+ (<span class=\"italic\">not</span>) <span class=\"italic\">have </span>+ past participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will have made</span> enough money to start my own firm.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " *Notice the position of <span class=\"italic\">not</span>. It comes between <span class=\"italic\">will</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "No don't phone Linda now, she'll be writing. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They'll be doing something wrong. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do I think we will be finished by tonight? Yes, I think we will have it finished by 5:00 p.m."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Maybe in five years time I'll have had enough of this job. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will have made enough money to start my own firm. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Third Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are four types of conditional sentences in English:<ol><li>Zero Conditional - to talk about certainty and facts</li><li>First Conditional - to talk about real possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Second Conditional - to talk about <span class=\"italic\">unreal</span> possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Third Conditional - to talk about unreal <span class=\"italic\">past</span> situations</li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the third conditional to talk about unreal situations in the past. <br/>These are things that did not happen in the past. You often use the third conditional to talk about regrets."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the third conditional:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Conditional Name</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Structure</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Third \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">would have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had stayed</span> at my last job I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would have worked</span> much less than I do now.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I had picked another place to work, I would not be anywhere near as fulfilled as I am at Corbin. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I had stayed at my last job I would have worked much less than I do now. Of course, I would have also been paid much less than I am now as well."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If they would have left the old manager in charge of the office, I would have left. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine you are the CEO of a company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain what your company does."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Select a company you like and write a business plan with future goals for your company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include short term and long term goals."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When expressing your goals, talk about what your company will have done and what they will be doing in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your company to your class in a short 5 minute presentation."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I create a business plan."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create future goals."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I express my goals using the Future Continuous and Future Perfect tenses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my company to the class."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who keeps close and secretly watches others "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You are not a spy, are you?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about colleagues."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "colleagues"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "partners from work"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Your colleagues are top-notch, the work is challenging and the job pays well."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "top notch"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the leading position"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Your colleagues are top-notch, the work is challenging and the job pays well."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "downside"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "discouraging or negative aspect "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Any downside?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be in charge"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to command, to lead"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If they left the old manager in charge of the office, I would have left. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "on the ball"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "be quick to understand or to react "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Our new boss is really on the ball."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "snowed under"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have so much work"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You are snowed under with paperwork."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le09ob07re1img01.jpg"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"_data": [], "type": "audio", "id": 1, "template_override": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn9le09ob07re2aud01", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "image": "engenn9le09ob07re2img01.jpg", "time": "0"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jill</span>:  So I was wondering what are your feelings about Corbin? Do you like working there?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Black suit</span>: You are not a spy, are you? Listen, if I had picked another place to work, I would not be anywhere near as fulfilled as I am at Corbin. It really is a good place to work. Your colleagues are top-notch, the work is challenging and the job pays well.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Jill</span>: Any downside?", "id": 1, "image": "engenn9le09ob07re2img01.jpg", "time": "100"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Black suit</span>: You are snowed under with paperwork. If I had stayed at my last job I would have worked much less than I do now. Of course, I would have also been paid much less than I am now as well. Maybe in five years time I'll have had enough of this job and I will have made enough money to start my own firm. That said, I am very satisfied here. Although, if they left the old manager in charge of the office, I would have left. He was terrible. Our new boss is really on the ball.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn9le09ob07re2img02.jpg", "time": "24000"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Black suit</span>: Just a sec ... Hello? Hi. Yep. No don't phone Linda now, she'll be writing. Uh huh. Yeah check in with accounting. They'll be doing something wrong. Uh huh. Do I think we will be finished by tonight? Yes, I think we will have it finished by 5:00 p.m. Bye.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Black suit</span>: Sorry. I have to go. What's your name?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Jill</span>: Jill.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Black suit</span>: Roger.  Good luck!", "id": 3, "image": "engenn9le09ob07re2img03.jpg", "time": "53300"}], "coverimg": "engenn9le09ob07re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about emotions, opinions and behavior in a work situation."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about what I will be doing or what I will have done. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about hypothetical situations in the past."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you think you have a good head for business? Why?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What kind of business would you like to start?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Planning for your business future."}], "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "template_override": 1, "questions": []}, {"_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mark has some really s